m; margin-left: -0.0785em; margin-right: 0.05em;&quot; class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border-color: currentcolor; display: inline-block; overflow: hidden; width: 0px; height: 2.7em;&quot; class=&quot;pstrut&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border-color: currentcolor; display: inline-block;&quot; class=&quot;sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border-color: currentcolor; font-family: KaTeX_Math; font-style: italic;&quot; class=&quot;mord mathnormal mtight&quot;&gt;p&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border-color: currentcolor; display: table-cell; min-width: 2px; vertical-align: bottom; width: 2px;&quot; class=&quot;vlist-s&quot;&gt;​&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border-color: currentcolor; display: table-row;&quot; class=&quot;vlist-r&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border-color: currentcolor; display: table-cell; position: relative; vertical-align: bottom; height: 0.2861em;&quot; class=&quot;vlist&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;border-color: currentcolor; display: block; height: 0px; position: relative;&quot; class=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;1557&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;1558&quot;&gt;Isso significa que, embora a probabilidade em si não varie de forma linear, o logaritmo das chances de ocorrer o evento varia linearmente com as variáveis de entrada&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;1724&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;fontSize=22;" vertex="1" parent="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="40" y="1360" width="1720" height="480" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="15" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Estimativa por&amp;nbsp; Máxima Verossimilhança&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(36, 36, 36); letter-spacing: -0.06px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Helvetica&quot;&gt;A regressão linear é um algoritmo de aprendizado supervisionado em aprendizado de máquina, amplamente utilizado para resolver problemas de regressão.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(36, 36, 36); letter-spacing: -0.06px; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;Na regressão linear, o objetivo é encontrar a equação linear que melhor se ajusta aos dados para descrever a relação entre as variáveis ​​de e&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;fontSize=22;" vertex="1" parent="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="40" y="1790" width="1720" height="370" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="16" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: rgb(63, 63, 63); font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans Text&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 22px; font-weight: normal;&quot;&gt;A regressão logística é preferível à regressão linear para problemas de classificação principalmente devido à natureza da variável de resposta qualitativa e à interpretação dos resultados como probabilidades. As fontes destacam as seguintes razões fundamentais:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: 1.5rem; font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans Text&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, sans-serif; margin-block-end: 0.75rem;&quot; data-start-index=&quot;261&quot; class=&quot;paragraph normal ng-star-inserted&quot;&gt;&lt;font&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot;&gt;• &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;261&quot;&gt;Previsões fora do intervalo de probabilidade:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;306&quot;&gt; Ao utilizar a regressão linear para uma resposta binária (0 ou 1), o modelo pode produzir estimativas &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;409&quot;&gt;fora do intervalo&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;426&quot;&gt;, resultando em probabilidades negativas ou superiores a 100%, o que não faz sentido matemático&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;522&quot;&gt;. A regressão logística resolve isso utilizando a &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;572&quot;&gt;função logística&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;588&quot;&gt;, que garante que a saída esteja sempre entre 0 e 1 para qualquer valor de entrada&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;670&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: 1.5rem; font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans Text&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, sans-serif; margin-block-end: 0.75rem;&quot; data-start-index=&quot;671&quot; class=&quot;paragraph normal ng-star-inserted&quot;&gt;&lt;font&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot;&gt;• &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;671&quot;&gt;Problemas com múltiplas classes:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;703&quot;&gt; A regressão linear não consegue acomodar naturalmente variáveis qualitativas com &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;785&quot;&gt;mais de duas classes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;805&quot;&gt;. Tentar codificar várias categorias como números (ex: 1, 2 e 3) implica uma &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;882&quot;&gt;ordem e uma distância arbitrária&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;914&quot;&gt; entre elas que não existem na realidade, como sugerir que a diferença entre a classe 1 e 2 é a mesma que entre a 2 e a 3&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;1036&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; font-stretch: normal; line-height: 1.5rem; font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans Text&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, sans-serif; margin-block-end: 0.75rem;&quot; data-start-index=&quot;1037&quot; class=&quot;paragraph normal ng-star-inserted&quot;&gt;&lt;font&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot;&gt;• &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;1037&quot;&gt;Inconsistência na codificação:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;1067&quot;&gt; Em problemas multiclasse, diferentes formas de atribuir números às categorias na regressão linear resultariam em modelos e previsões completamente distintos e inconsistentes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;1241&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;font-style: normal; font-variant: normal; font-size-adjust: none; font-kerning: auto; font-optical-sizing: auto; font-feature-settings: normal; font-variation-settings: normal; font-weight: 400; font-stretch: normal; line-height: 1.5rem; font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans Text&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, sans-serif; letter-spacing: normal; margin-block-end: 0.75rem;&quot; data-start-index=&quot;1242&quot; class=&quot;paragraph normal ng-star-inserted&quot;&gt;&lt;font&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot;&gt;• &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;1242&quot;&gt;Ajuste inadequado aos dados:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;1270&quot;&gt; A regressão logística é capaz de capturar a gama de probabilidades de forma mais eficaz, produzindo uma &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;1375&quot;&gt;curva em formato de &quot;S&quot;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;1398&quot;&gt; que reflete melhor a transição entre as classes do que a linha reta da regressão linear&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot; class=&quot;ng-star-inserted&quot; data-start-index=&quot;1486&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;fontSize=22;" vertex="1" parent="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="-1400" y="-40" width="1360" height="500" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
            </root>
        </mxGraphModel>
    </diagram>
</mxfile>